            <div xml:id="d603">

                <pb facs="0749" n="655" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg655"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00 Johnson Electoral Mission/127:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-11-14T17:00:00-05:45">November 14, 1930—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>155. The evacuation of the bulk of the personnel of the electoral mission and
                    additional marines temporarily ashore in Nicaragua to assist in the preservation
                    of order during the electoral period began on November 4th and will be completed
                    when the <hi rendition="#italic">Rochester</hi> leaves Corinto for the Canal
                    Zone on November 17th. The total electoral personnel thus evacuated embraces 36
                    officers and 536 enlisted and 153 additional marines. There remain 18 officers
                    and 24 enlisted to complete the work of the mission.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
